note Exercism-style exercise "rotational-cipher": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/rotational-cipher
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note rotate writes s into o with every letter shifted key places along the alphabet (keeping its
note case, wrapping z to a) and every other byte unchanged; returns the length.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/rotational-cipher
om2
fn rotate s view uchar * key ulong o edit uchar * to ulong
k = uchar rem key 26
for i ulong len s
c = get s i
if and ge c 65 le c 90
c = add 65 rem add sub c 65 k 26
else
if and ge c 97 le c 122
c = add 97 rem add sub c 97 k 26
end
end
put o i c
end
ret len s
end
